<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antioquia Department</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antioquia is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of north-western Colombia in the Central and Western Cordilleras; its capital is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medellin">Medellín</a>. In the colonial era it was a major source of gold, worked by enslaved Africans and free prospectors. In the 19th century it was a sovereign state of the Colombian federation, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> farming and the commerce of Medellín later made it the leading industrial region of Colombia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antioquia-department.jpg" alt="Antioquia Department" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stiven8807 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paisaje_desde_la_vereda_la_esperanza(@stiven1331).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
